    <bpmn:process id="W_W5177" name="W5177. Disaster Relief Supply Forecasting &amp; Category Inventory Staging Plan" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of typhoon season (Q2); weather bureau PAGASA tracking major storm warning
Frequency: Seasonal + storm event-driven
Volume: Staging plan covering 4 regional DCs and 200 stores
Owner: Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Participants: Category Managers (VS-01), Logistics Manager (VS-06), DC Operations (VS-04)
Source: workflow W5177 — Disaster Relief Supply Forecasting &amp; Category Inventory Staging Plan</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5177_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5177_Lane1" name="Director of Supply Chain Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5177_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5177_Start3" name="Start of typhoon season (Q2); weather bureau PAGASA tracking major storm warning">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5177_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5177_Task4" name="Analyze historic storm tracks and geographic store vulnerabilities (e.g. East…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Analyze historic storm tracks and geographic store vulnerabilities (e.g. East Coast Luzon, Visayas).
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5177_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5177_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5177_Task5" name="Model relief demand: forecast quantity spikes for galvanized iron (GI) roof…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Model relief demand: forecast quantity spikes for galvanized iron (GI) roof sheets, plywood, nails, cement, flashlights, batteries, and portable generators.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5177_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5177_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5177_Task6" name="Draft the Disaster Staging Plan: define inventory reserve targets for safety…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Draft the Disaster Staging Plan: define inventory reserve targets for safety stock levels at DC hubs (Mindanao, Visayas, Luzon).
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5177_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5177_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5177_Task7" name="Execute inventory stock transfers to pre-position forecasted SKUs at regional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Execute inventory stock transfers to pre-position forecasted SKUs at regional DCs prior to landfall.
Responsible (R): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Accountable (A): Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5177_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5177_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5177_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5177_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-770 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Material Allocation, Disaster Kit Assembly &amp; Staging Operations (PA-180.1).) | - CTL-770: Staging Plan approved by VP Supply Chain; safety stock thresholds configured in ERP.
Owner: Director of Supply Chain Planning / S&amp;OP Manager (VS-127)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
