    <bpmn:process id="W_W5178" name="W5178. Emergency Building Materials (Galvanized Sheets, Nails, Lumber) Priority Allocation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: LGU State of Calamity declaration; high supply constraints post-landfall
Frequency: Event-driven per storm landfall
Volume: ~5–10 allocation events annually
Owner: Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Participants: DC Manager (VS-04), Category Buyers (VS-03), Store Managers
Source: workflow W5178 — Emergency Building Materials (Galvanized Sheets, Nails, Lumber) Priority Allocation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5178_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5178_Lane1" name="Director of Inventory Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5178_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5178_Start3" name="LGU State of Calamity declaration; high supply constraints post-landfall">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5178_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5178_Task4" name="Identify depleted relief SKUs and aggregate outstanding backorders from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Identify depleted relief SKUs and aggregate outstanding backorders from affected stores.
Responsible (R): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5178_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5178_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5178_Task5" name="Implement ERP inventory lock: reserve incoming and existing stocks of GI…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Implement ERP inventory lock: reserve incoming and existing stocks of GI sheets, lumber, and fasteners at DCs for disaster regions.
Responsible (R): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5178_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5178_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5178_Task6" name="Apply allocation rules: distribute stock based on LGU damage severity ratings…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Apply allocation rules: distribute stock based on LGU damage severity ratings (NDRRMC briefs) and store waitlists.
Responsible (R): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5178_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5178_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5178_Task7" name="Coordinate fast-track PO release to local building material manufacturers…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Coordinate fast-track PO release to local building material manufacturers (VS-03) with emergency lead times.
Responsible (R): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5178_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5178_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5178_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5178_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-770 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Material Allocation, Disaster Kit Assembly &amp; Staging Operations (PA-180.1).) | - CTL-770: Allocation adjustments require sign-off from Director of Inventory; changes audited.
Owner: Director of Inventory Management / Supply Chain Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
