    <bpmn:process id="W_W5179" name="W5179. Disaster Relief Home Rebuilding Kit Kitting &amp; Staging" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Disaster Staging Plan activation (W5177); NGO partner request
Frequency: Seasonal + event-driven
Volume: ~5,000–10,000 kits assembled annually
Owner: DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Participants: Kitting Associates, Packaging team (VS-111), Procurement, CSR (VS-152)
Source: workflow W5179 — Disaster Relief Home Rebuilding Kit Kitting &amp; Staging</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5179_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5179_Lane1" name="DC Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5179_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5179_Start3" name="Disaster Staging Plan activation (W5177); NGO partner request">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5179_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5179_Task4" name="Define Bill of Materials (BOM) for the &#x27;BuildRight Home Rebuilding Kit&#x27; (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Define Bill of Materials (BOM) for the &#x27;BuildRight Home Rebuilding Kit&#x27; (e.g. 10 GI sheets, 3 pcs lumber, 5kg nails, hammer, handsaw, tarpaulin).
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5179_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5179_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5179_Task5" name="Set up the kitting line in DC staging zones: configure workspaces, arrange…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Set up the kitting line in DC staging zones: configure workspaces, arrange packaging crates, and stage components.
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5179_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5179_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5179_Task6" name="Execute kit assembly: pick components, bundle lumber/sheets, pack hand tools…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Execute kit assembly: pick components, bundle lumber/sheets, pack hand tools, and shrink-wrap the consolidated kit (VS-92).
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5179_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5179_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5179_Task7" name="Label kits with barcodes, technical descriptions, and safety instructions…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Label kits with barcodes, technical descriptions, and safety instructions; stage in outbound lane for dispatch.
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Accountable (A): DC Operations Manager (VS-04)
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5179_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5179_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5179_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5179_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-770 (ensure controlled execution — Emergency Material Allocation, Disaster Kit Assembly &amp; Staging Operations (PA-180.1).) | - CTL-770: Kit weight checked on exit scale; completed kits inspected by DC QA supervisor.
Owner: DC Operations Manager (VS-04)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
